WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.850
Do you think that we're going to find out
that the name Black Widow is like getting

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:04.850
belts in karate?

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.171
Like you start out as a White Widow, and then
you're a White Widow with a yellow tip, and

00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:10.200
then you're a Yellow Widow?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.200
Oh. I hope so.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:17.929
Nina, what are the biggest questions we want
answered in Black Widow?

00:00:17.929 --> 00:00:23.630
So we've gotten so many tiny, tantalizing
looks at her past through flashbacks and other

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.630
movies.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.520
I think it was Age of Ultron where we kind
of got the most look at it, where the Scarlet

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.780
Witch, or rather Wanda at the time, brought
out everybody's worst memories.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.550
But I'm really curious to see.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.170
We're going to get her entire backstory for
the first time, as you said, in the entire

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.170
MCU.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:45.640
And I'm also really excited and have a lot
of questions about the character of Yelena,

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:50.559
her sister, played by Florence Pugh, because
I think she's a phenomenal actress and a great

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:51.770
addition to the MCU.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:57.320
So I'm really curious to learn more about
Nat and also her family dynamics, her dynamic

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.320
with Yelena.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.440
I think it's going to be really exciting.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.440
Yeah.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:05.560
So you want to learn all about the family
backstory for this character, who we've known

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.520
for over 10 years now.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.520
Yeah.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.610
You've got Scarlett Johannson playing her.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:14.140
It seems like it's been a little bit of a
waste to have such a talented...

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.020
Someone who was nominated for two Academy
Awards in a year recently, to not be able

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:20.479
to play the more emotional side of Natasha.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:27.320
So I think it has the potential to be a more
kind of family and relationship-centric Marvel

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.320
movie.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.320
Yeah.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.320
Cool.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:31.320
I agree.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.899
I think that that's a really good point, that
all we've known about her is that she was

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:37.210
raised in this red room and there's some program.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:41.520
And we know that the plot is going to surround
this program, but we don't know much else

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.210
about her as a human being.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:45.210
Right.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:49.600
So I think that, yeah, I think that's a really
good bunch of questions to answer.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:50.600
Yeah.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:51.780
Tom, what do you think?

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.790
What are the questions you want answered in
Black Widow?

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.820
I'm also thrilled to see it.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.770
I'm excited to get a lot of questions answered.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:06.469
I want to find out what the Kessel Run is,
and how Black Widow managed to make it in

00:02:06.469 --> 00:02:08.450
less than 12 parsecs.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.690
It was hard to do, but she managed it somehow.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.530
So I think that you're right.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:17.120
I mean, in addition it would probably be helpful
if they explain how she came up with the name

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.510
Black Widow.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.310
I mean, you don't just come up with a name
like that.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.450
You don't just have a name.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.500
No, you're going through customs and you're
like, "I'm a widow."

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.880
And they're like, "But what color?"

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.920
And then she looks at the jacket that she's
wearing.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.920
Right.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.560
Well, it also seems like a nickname that someone
would give to you.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:43.280
Like kind of the Kill Bill, like assassin
nicknames, like Black Mamba and Rattlesnake,

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.280
like a dangerous snake.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.980
I'm like, Black Widow doesn't sound like something
you make up for yourself.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.160
That would be kind of lame.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.350
Legitimate.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.840
And that's exactly the sort of thing that
I'm curious about.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.160
Did Black Widow's friend, Professor Xavier,
lose his hair naturally or was it during a

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.510
fight with Apocalypse?

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:04.580
Is Black Widow related to Ernst Stavro Blofeld?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.620
Does it turn out that they were brothers all
along?

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.000
I'm really worried about this movie.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.350
I'm excited for it.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:15.600
I think that Scarlett Johannson has made the
character so much more interesting than I

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.190
ever thought that she was in the comics.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:22.930
She's added a lot of depth to it, and so did
Joss Whedon, so did all of the writers.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:31.370
But I'm very concerned about the idea of the
precedent of, we need to fill in every blank

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.460
in these stories.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.340
That's a good point.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:41.680
I can't think of a time when that's made a
story more satisfying, at least not in recent

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:42.680
history.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.680
Godfather Part II.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:44.680
I thought you're going to say three.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.120
I was so excited.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.360
I was so excited.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:53.420
Well, no, you raise a really good point there,
too, because this is probably, aside from

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.380
Captain Marvel, this is...

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.380
Well, no.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.280
I'm already contradicting myself.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.590
There've been a few prequels, right?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.860
A few jumps in time.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:08.300
Captain America, the First Avenger obviously
took place before Iron Man 1, 2, Thor and

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.300
Incredible Hulk.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.460
So Captain America went back in time, but
that was for a brand new character.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:18.829
So it's filling in tons of blanks, but still
telling a new story wrapped in the Marvel.

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:20.310
Yeah, go ahead.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:23.730
Just very specifically, with Black Widow,
I think that a lot of what makes her work

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.120
is that you don't know stuff about her.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.590
You know, I think that a lot of the intrigue
comes from the mystery.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:35.590
We kind of get to imagine for ourselves with
what happened in Budapest.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:39.210
Isn't that the Patton Oswalt joke, where he's
like, "I don't want to know the backstory

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.210
of my favorite characters.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.450
I just want to like them."

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:42.450
Yeah.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.620
Darth Vader's a little kid.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:44.620
Yeah.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.240
That's a good point.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.440
Yeah.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.930
I've watched a couple videos recently about
Cruella.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.010
I haven't watched Cruella yet, because I don't-

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.010
Nor have it.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:05:03.060
... care about how the villain from 101 Dalmatians
became a mean lady and apparently...

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:07.060
I'm not going to give away spoilers, in case
anyone wants to watch it, but apparently the

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:14.380
origin for her distaste for Dalmatians is
pretty amazing.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:17.800
I've seen a clip of it and it looks insane.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:21.150
It's one of those things where you don't need
to know.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.150
You don't need to know.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:27.760
And so I agree that there's definitely a danger
here with Black Widow, in terms of, I want

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.330
to see the family dynamic.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.010
I want to know more about her and her family
and how she fits into that.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.040
I did a little research.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:38.200
It looks like, and maybe this is common knowledge,
maybe it's not, obviously we've been preoccupied

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:43.370
over the last year, so I haven't dived deep
into what this movie is going to have.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:46.610
But apparently all the family members are
not her biological family.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.610
Right.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:48.610
Right.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.610
These are adoptive family members.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.991
And so it still will be interesting to learn
more, and I know that there's going to be

00:05:51.991 --> 00:05:53.610
some flashback scenes.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:58.870
I think Tom raises some good points, that
if we get too into the weeds about the details

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:05.440
of every in and out of this character's history,
it's going to be a little bit...

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.380
It's going to fill in too many blanks, right?

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:15.320
Like when they finally published Wolverine
Origin, back in the, I want to say late '90s.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.580
Terrific point.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.580
Yeah.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.400
That's a bad comic book.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.400
Sorry.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.400
It's not good.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.570
I don't care about seeing Wolverine as a little
kid.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:24.730
I don't care.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:31.250
I mean, in that same vein, sorry to disappoint,
I think Solo is a bad movie for the same reason.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.640
Yeah.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.190
I don't need to know why his name is Han Solo,
is my point.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.470
I think the movie is fine, but I didn't need
to know where his name came from.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:41.610
That was not something that ever kept me up
at night.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.670
So I hope Black Widow doesn't go in one of
those directions.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:49.040
I think there's ways that it can be a good
prequel and actually flesh out this really

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.040
interesting character.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:53.070
But the timing is also weird, because she's
already dead.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.070
Exactly.

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.070
In the MCU.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:56.830
And that's so jarring.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:59.790
I know that there was a huge delay, obviously,
because of the pandemic, but still.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:03.850
But even without delay, it still would've
come out after she'd been dead for several

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:04.850
months.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:05.850
Exactly.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:09.340
So it's so weird to be like, well, this character's
back, but she's not going to be an any future

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:10.730
set installments.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.440
That's very jarring.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:16.010
Do you think that we're going to find out
that the name Black Widow is like getting

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:17.290
belts in karate?

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:21.169
Like you start out as a White Widow, and then
you're a White Widow with a yellow tip, and

00:07:21.169 --> 00:07:22.320
then you're a Yellow Widow?

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:23.320
Oh.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:24.320
I hope so.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.440
That would be awesome.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.800
I'm actually really-

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:27.800
Watch out.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:28.800
She's a Brown Widow.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.400
She's pretty good.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.030
She's almost achieved the level of Black Widow.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:37.930
How great would it be if it turned out that
this whole movie just takes place in a strip

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:43.380
mall in Russia, where somebody is teaching
little girls TaeKwonDo.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.560
The Russian equivalent of Tiger Schulmann?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.620
It's just weekends.

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.720
It says Russia, but it looks exactly like
New Jersey.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:54.350
You're like, I think that's just Cherry Hill.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:56.320
I've been there.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:57.320
Yeah.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.730
A Domino's guy just drove by.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:04.010
What's going on?

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.640
There's a Guitar Center right in the background.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:07.910
Why didn't they just get rid of that in post?

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:10.130
I was just going to say, Guitar-ski Center-ski.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:15.930
So, one of the things that I want to see answered,
Tom brought it up.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.960
I do want to know what happened in Budapest.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:22.010
It's one of those things, those parts of her
character, just to remind everyone, we first

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:24.020
hear about Budapest and the first Avengers
movie.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:28.580
I think they bring it up once or twice in
a couple of the other Avengers movies where-

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.180
She and Hawkeye talk about it a lot.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:31.180
Right.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.870
Black Widow says, "This reminds me of Budapest."

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:37.750
Hawkeye says, "You and I have very different
recollections of Budapest."

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:43.650
I feel like we're probably not going to get
a flashback to Budapest, but I think it would

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:49.090
be a nice little fill in the blank there,
to kind of give us a sense for this thing

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:50.090
that they've talked about.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:53.610
It's iconic enough that we all are talking
about it, even though we have no idea what

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:54.920
happens.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:09:03.750
And it's not in the same realm of this is
how Black Widow got her jacket.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:07.810
This is how Black Widow got her weapons on
her arm.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:10.120
This is how Black Widow got her haircut.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.120
Like we don't care.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:16.650
But I do think that that's a nice piece of
backstory that I would love to kind of get

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.660
filled in, personally.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.850
That's one of the questions I'd like to see
answered, personally.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:23.980
I hope we get a haircut montage.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.880
Like the SNL Black Widow trailer?

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:28.610
Where they give her a make-over?

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:29.610
Yeah.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:30.610
There you go.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:31.610
That's perfect.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:32.610
What if it's just a romantic comedy?

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:37.140
What if it feels exactly like 27 Dresses,
but it's a Marvel movie?

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:39.850
I would love a Marvel romantic comedy.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:44.260
She's trying different catsuits on.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:47.480
There's a voiceover where it's like, "Black
Widow is too busy saving the world to find

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:48.480
love."

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.480
Yeah.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.920
We're going to talk about this eventually,
about She Hulk.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:56.880
This is a different topic, but that's literally
one of the things I want them to do with She

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:02.980
Hulk, where she's a lawyer, she's a She Hulk,
where is she going to find love?

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:03.980
Right.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:07.540
Can a woman have it all, when you're busy
saving the world and trying to establish a

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.670
successful law practice?

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.220
A question as old as time itself.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:11.220
Yeah.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.220
I don't know.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:13.220
Yeah.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:16.490
I basically want Liz Lemon as She Hulk.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:21.260
And instead of running a variety show, she's
doing a superhero themed law practice.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:22.260
I love it.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:27.330
In a lot of ways, the giant sky portal above
New York is like another character in the

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:30.980
show, which is really great.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.440
Yes, exactly.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:33.440
Perfect.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.790
So yeah, those are all the things I definitely
think...

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:42.690
I think we all agree here that as far as questions
are concerned, we want answers to questions.

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:46.640
We want to know more about this character,
but we don't want to know everything.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:51.580
And I think one of the things that I can say
with confidence is that with Black Widow,

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.230
it's a Marvel Studios movie.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:56.460
We don't have to worry that they're going
to shoe horn in an origin story for every

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:59.149
element of her character.

00:10:59.149 --> 00:11:00.570
With Solo, right?

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:04.140
You brought up Solo not being a great movie,
and I think that most people would probably

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.140
agree.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.610
There's a lot about it that works.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:10.450
There's a lot about it that maybe doesn't
quite work.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:14.420
And I think that a lot of that has to do with
the fact that the production had to basically

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.870
change hands midway through.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:20.390
They weren't sure what they were doing when
they first started.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:22.990
The studio wanted this, the filmmakers wanted
that.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:25.740
Then they bring in Ron Howard and then they
do all these re-shoots.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:26.740
Right.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.860
I mean, that movie had a lot of \troubled
production issues.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:32.940
And Black Widow, also, the anticipation is
so high because we've been waiting so long.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:36.290
We were supposed to see this movie over a
year ago.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.290
Yeah.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.140
And even that was way too long.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.750
Exactly.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:43.350
Right.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:46.000
I think it'll be pretty cool.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.000
Yeah.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.000
I agree.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.000
I'm excited to see it.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.000
Who's Taskmaster?

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.310
What's happening with Taskmaster?

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.029
I want to know that part.

00:11:53.029 --> 00:11:54.310
That part I'm excited about.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:55.310
Yeah.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:59.750
So before we sign off on this one, let's talk
about that.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:06.820
One of our coworkers at Looper, Sarah, who
works in the scripts department, she was talking

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:12.450
with the rest of the team, and I believe she
was the one who brought up the idea that,

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:16.930
potential spoiler alert, She predicts that
it's going to be Rachel Weisz's character.

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:18.589
Of course, it's going to be Rachel Weisz's
character.

00:12:18.589 --> 00:12:19.589
Okay.

00:12:19.589 --> 00:12:20.589
Do we all pretty much think that this is what's
happening?

00:12:20.589 --> 00:12:21.589
Are we children?

00:12:21.589 --> 00:12:24.940
I'm sorry, I thought that we were having an
adult conversation.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:28.190
If it's not Rachel Weisz's character, I will
walk out of my own living room or wherever

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.190
I watch this film.

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:30.770
I mean, that's the thing, right?

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:33.899
It's the same thing with who is the Power
Broker, right?

00:12:33.899 --> 00:12:37.070
It's like, if it's not Sharon Carter, who
else is left?

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:39.940
It has to be someone who hasn't been shown
in this.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.250
And so far we know it's not David Harbour.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:44.120
He doesn't fit in that suit.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:48.270
It's probably not Florence Pugh, because they're
probably getting her ready to be the next

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:49.270
Black Widow.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:52.330
I've got a little Yelena Funko Pop behind
me, actually.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.240
They're already marketing her as a new superhero.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.170
There you go.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:57.870
Black Widow 2.

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:03.370
And so then you've got Rachel Weisz's character
who is the mother figure.

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.950
Yeah.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:09.940
And what better storyline is there for the
mother figure to betray her children, right?

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.160
Naturally.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.680
Like we've all gone through.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:13.680
Sure.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.200
We've all fought our mother in the same way.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:17.580
That's a classic story.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:20.100
It's so relatable.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.100
Yeah.

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:24.260
That's what I like most about this idea, is
how relatable it is.

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:28.760
That's why I watch Marvel movies, is for the
relate-ability.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:32.480
So I guess that's the better question then,
since we're all pretty much on board with

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:38.430
this being the reveal, I guess we hope that
the reveal is handled in a revealing and exciting

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:39.430
way.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:40.430
Yeah.

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:44.769
I hope it's not quite as clumsy as some of
the things that we found lacking in Falcon

00:13:44.769 --> 00:13:46.960
and Winter Soldier's kind of bigger reveal.

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:52.529
So I'm hoping Cate Shortland, the director,
who is kind of like an indie director...

00:13:52.529 --> 00:13:54.670
I just looked her up and I'm not familiar
with a ton of her work.

00:13:54.670 --> 00:14:01.839
So I'm curious to see kind of how she handles
this story and this very likely reveal.

00:14:01.839 --> 00:14:08.080
I mean, I guess I hope it's not her, because
it seems like the obvious choice, but I don't

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:10.860
know who else it could be.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:16.649
Maybe it'll be some other character that we're
introduced to that we are not even aware of,

00:14:16.649 --> 00:14:19.430
and it'll be some super big, awesome, secret
surprise.

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:20.430
That would be great.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:21.430
I would love that.

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:22.430
Yeah.

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:25.660
I think it was really brave that they decided
to go with an indie director, especially after

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:27.400
Crystal Skull sucked so bad.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:30.070
You did it.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:33.630
You did it, Tom.

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:39.070
We got to freeze frame him like Breakfast
Club style.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:42.430
Thanks for joining us.

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:45.839
Please hit like and subscribe so you don't
miss a single new episode.

